TYPES
- Conductor: copper (most common); aluminum possible for larger sizes
- Insulation: PVC, XLPE, or thermoset (temperature rating 60°C / 75°C / 90°C)
- Installation: free air, conduit, cable tray, buried, or bundled

VARIABLES
- A = cross-sectional area (mm²)
- I = continuous current (A)
- R = resistance per unit length (Ω/km)
- ΔT = temperature rise
- n = number of current-carrying conductors
- Ta = ambient temperature (°C)

FUNDAMENTALS
- Ampacity limited by I²R heating; heat must dissipate without exceeding insulation rating
- Larger A → lower R → higher allowable I (approximately I ∝ √A for same conditions)
- Derating required for high ambient temperature, bundling, conduit fill, or altitude
- Voltage drop (IR drop) often governs long runs more than ampacity
- Official reference: NEC Table 310.15(B)(16) (or local equivalent / IEC 60364) for exact values under stated conditions
- Chart above is approximate visual summary only; use code tables + derating factors for design
